/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Ransomware is a type of malware that permanently blocks access to the victim's personal data unless a "ransom" is paid. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (While some simple ransomware may lock the system without damaging any files, more advanced malware uses a technique called cryptoviral extortion. It encrypts the victim's files, making them inaccessible, and demands a ransom payment to decrypt them. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In a properly implemented cryptoviral extortion attack, recovering the files without the decryption key is an intractable problem, and difficult-to-trace digital currencies such as paysafecard or Bitcoin and other cryptocurrencies are used for the ransoms, making tracing and prosecuting the perpetrators difficult.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
