290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Even though the records of cryptocurrency transactions are publicly available on the cryptographic ledger of blockchain the identify of the individuals involved is anonymous. Attackers often obfuscate funds to evade detection. This makes tracking those transactions difficult. Alongside having multiple wallet with each of them having a different address this makes this even more difficult. It is possible however, as evidenced by the $2.3 million worth of bitcoin which was recovered from Colonials ransom payment by the FBI, supported by blockchain analysis company, Chainalysis.)
/E (Even though the records of cryptocurrency transactions are publicly available on the cryptographic ledger of blockchain the identify of the individuals involved is anonymous. Attackers often obfuscate funds to evade detection. This makes tracking those transactions difficult. Alongside having multiple wallet with each of them having a different address this makes this even more difficult. It is possible however, as evidenced by the $2.3 million worth of bitcoin which was recovered from Colonials ransom payment by the FBI, supported by blockchain analysis company, Chainalysis.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
